 ("portion_declared", "speech", "the portion declared — 'and the LORD said to Aaron: in their land you shall not inherit, and you shall have no portion among them; I am your portion and your inheritance among the children of Israel; and to the sons of Levi, behold, I have given all the tithe in Israel for an inheritance in exchange for their service which they serve, the service of the tent of meeting; and the children of Israel shall no more come near the tent of meeting to bear sin, to die; and the Levite, he shall serve the service of the tent of meeting, and they shall bear their iniquity — an everlasting statute for your generations — and among the children of Israel they shall inherit no inheritance; for the tithe of the children of Israel which they lift as a terumah to the LORD I have given to the Levites for an inheritance; therefore I have said to them: among the children of Israel they shall inherit no inheritance' (Num 18:20-24) — 'I am your portion' (Onkelos: the gifts I have given you, they are); the exclusion table from 26:53 (Sifrei 119:1); the wage conditioned on service; 'in exchange' the Torah's two seats",
  HE(18, 20, 24, "and the LORD said to Aaron: in their land you shall not inherit, and you shall have no portion among them; I am your portion and your inheritance"), WIT(18, 20, 24), "Num 18:20-24; Onkelos Num 18:20-24; Sifrei Bamidbar 119:1-5; Yevamot 86a:2, 86b:1-2; Rosh Hashanah 12b:3; Temurah 3a:9; Mishnah Ma'aser Sheni 5:14; Num 26:53-55; Deut 10:9, 18:2; Josh 13:14; Ezek 44:28", "num_18_priest_levite_dues (STEP_Nm_18_20 through STEP_Nm_18_24; claims KR18A-09, KR18A-10)", SUB % ("the-levites", "inheritance_barred (the BLOCK on Aaron, 18:20, and on the Levites, 18:23-24 — no inheritance in the land), tithe_granted (the standing status on the Levites — all the tithe in Israel, in exchange for their service)"), ["portion", "tithe", "condition"]),
 ("tithe_of_the_tithe_commanded", "speech", "the tithe of the tithe commanded — 'and the LORD spoke to Moses saying: and to the Levites you shall speak and say to them: when you take from the children of Israel the tithe which I have given you from them for your inheritance, you shall lift from it a terumah of the LORD, a tithe from the tithe; and your terumah shall be reckoned to you as the grain from the threshing floor and as the fullness of the winepress; so you too shall lift the terumah of the LORD from all your tithes... from all its best, its hallowed part from it; and you shall say to them: when you lift its best from it, it shall be reckoned to the Levites as the produce of the threshing floor and the produce of the winepress; and you may eat it in every place, you and your household, for it is your wage in exchange for your service in the tent of meeting; and you shall bear no sin by reason of it when you lift its best from it, and the holy things of the children of Israel you shall not profane, and you shall not die' (Num 18:25-32) — a tenth of the tenth = one in a hundred; 15:20's pointer PAID; by estimate and thought; the thresholds; 'from it' free for the mourner; the wage; 'you shall not die' the priests' words (Lev 8:35, 10:6-9)",
  HE(18, 25, 32, "and the LORD spoke to Moses saying: and to the Levites you shall speak and say to them"), WIT(18, 25, 32), "Num 18:25-32; Onkelos Num 18:25-32; Sifrei Bamidbar 120:1, 121:1, 122:1; Menachot 54b:11; Beitzah 13b:3-7; Berakhot 47a:15-47b:1; Bekhorot 58b:11, 59a:1, 26b:18; Bava Metzia 22a:8, 88b:7; Yevamot 86a:9, 89b:2; Mishnah Terumot 1:5, 2:4, 4:3; Mishnah Ma'aserot 1:5-8; Neh 10:39; Num 15:20", "num_18_priest_levite_dues (STEP_Nm_18_25 through STEP_Nm_18_32; claims KR18A-11, KR18A-12)", SUB % ("the-levites", "terumah_of_the_tithe_owed (the standing status on the Levites — a tenth of the tenth to Aaron the priest, from the best, by estimate)"), ["fraction", "reckoned_as", "the_best"]),
